  "contract": "docs/GATE-CONTRACT.md [GC-A27] NN18: warm --to check and each fixed setup stage stay inside the host's budget. A null budget FAILS NN18 on that host (\"no budget measured\"), it never passes. A budget is only ever lowered, and only from a new measured run.",
  "method": "Provisional ceiling (EGM, 2026-11-06, adopted by Adrian): each value is the best measured optimized-state time x1.25. It is lowered per window to a noise-based margin (median of repeated runs plus measured run-to-run spread, with a millisecond floor) once repeated runs exist; values only ever go down. Only a value measured on that host and workload counts; a null fails NN18. Sources: fixture warm check 3.6 s (2026-11-05 12:47Z, 37 of 39 rows hit); RightKit warm check 7.2 s; HeardRight warm check 5.3 s; Pulse compile 70.9 s (warm: 90 of 95 compile rows cached, so it is a warm-compile budget, not cold); fixture resident verify 50 ms, metadata hit 75-100 ms, dependency digest 0.45 s (fixture only). Earlier text describing median-of-worst-runs x1.25 is superseded.",
  "stageLines": {
    "ownership": "the runner's launch time -> the first `build ownership held|joined` line; 0 for a run that takes no lease",
    "snapshotSync": "the ownership line (else the launch time) -> the `snapshot <dir> is commit <sha> tree <sha> (written=...` line",
    "planning": "the `rightkit-gate: --to <stage> for <sha12>: ...` line -> the `<n> scan(s) for <m> changed file(s) vs <sha12>; class A scans <j> at a time` line",
    "dependencyStep": "that plan line -> the first `snapshot dependencies root=` line"
  },
